The static variable is a variable that retains its value throughout the execution of the program. It is declared using the keyword 'static'. When a static variable is declared inside a function, it retains its value between function calls.

Here is an example of a static variable in C:

#include <stdio.h>
void myFunction() {
static int x = 0; // Declare a static variable
x++; // Increment the value of x
printf("x = %d\n", x);
}
int main() {
